{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/et8h4b","slideIndex":5,"text":"The 2016 file contains a 286.7 mm gridded estimate on 3 October and 232 cells above 167.1 mm. Met Éireann lists 167.1 mm at Killarney as the highest daily rainfall in 2016 on 3 October; its October summary describes 2016 as mainly anticyclonic and predominantly dry. A grid estimate is not a station observation, so this flags a conflict for sensitivity review rather than proving the grid is wrong. The whole date is omitted from the primary comparison pending clarification. Sources: https://www.met.ie/index.php/climate/weather-extreme-records ; https://www.met.ie/climate-statement-for-october-2021 ; https://clidata.met.ie/cli/grids_daily/"}
